  "id": "urban_s1_s2",
  "summary": "Urban detection by Sentinel-1/Sentinel-2 data fusion using openEO.",
  "description": "Detects built-up areas by combining Sentinel-1 GRD backscatter with Sentinel-2 vegetation and moisture masks. Each pixel falls through a four-way priority cascade: dense vegetation (NDVI > 0.5) and water (NDMI > 0) are rendered as Sentinel-2 true colour, remaining pixels bright in VH or VV (> 0.2) are rendered as Sentinel-1 false colour and read as built-up, and everything else falls back to a darkened true colour. Testing the optical masks first is what stops the radar threshold from misreading vegetation and water as buildings. Converted from the Sentinel Hub Urban Detection evalscript by Monja B. \u0160ebela."
}